Rule 5 (If out is a tuple, it should contain two tensors to avoid TypeError)
{v_3 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_3.len = 2
>>
Rule 9 (If dim is provided, it must be within the valid range to avoid IndexError. Multiplication is not allowed in the arith_factor, so the negative value is passed directly as a negative number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 * ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 14 (If out is provided and it's a tuple, the tuple length must be 2)
{v_1 : tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 20 (If dim is None, all dimensions must be non-zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 22 (If dim is provided, it must be within the valid range to avoid IndexError)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (0 - ndim(v_1)) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
